+The suite starts several test processes in one CI job. The original fixture asked the operating
+system for a free port, closed the probe, and later reopened the real listener on the returned
+number. A competing process could claim that number in between, producing the `EADDRINUSE`
+signature in `ci.log`.
 
-Run `npm test`. A competitor listener acquires the probed port before the application listener, so
-the pre-fix fixture fails deterministically with `EADDRINUSE`. The retained CI log shows the same
-signature from two shards.
+The test now asks the actual listener to bind port `0`. After the listening callback fires, it reads
+the operating-system-assigned port from `server.address().port`. Run `npm test`; concurrent
+independent test processes are the relevant regression check.
